<section class="section">
  <div class="container container-narrow">
    <h1>Privacy policy</h1>
    <p class="muted">Last updated: 20 September 2026</p>

    <div class="prose">
      <h2>What we collect</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>Your name, mobile number, email address and business name.</li>
        <li>Your district and delivery address, where relevant to your store.</li>
        <li>Order details, payment references and billing history.</li>
        <li>Support tickets you open with us, and our replies.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Why we collect it</h2>
      <ul>
        <li>To build and run the website you ordered.</li>
        <li>To verify mobile wallet payments such as bKash, Nagad and Rocket by hand.</li>
        <li>To raise invoices and keep accounting records.</li>
        <li>To answer your support requests and contact you about your account.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>Who we share it with</h2>
      <p>
        We do not sell your data. We share it only where it is necessary to deliver the service:
        with a domain registrar when registering your domain, with your chosen payment provider
        when processing a payment, and with a courier partner if your store ships orders.
      </p>

      <h2>How long we keep it</h2>
      <p>
        Billing records are kept for as long as accounting law requires. Support tickets are kept
        for three years. You can ask us to delete your account details once there are no
        outstanding invoices.
      </p>

      <h2>Your rights</h2>
      <p>
        You can ask to see, correct or delete the personal data we hold about you by writing to
        <a href="mailto:<%= settings.supportEmail || 'support@woohelperpro.com' %>"><%= settings.supportEmail || 'support@woohelperpro.com' %></a>.
        We will respond within 30 days.
      </p>

      <h2>Security</h2>
      <p>
        Passwords are stored as salted hashes — we never keep a readable copy. Access to customer
        records inside our admin panel is restricted by role and every change is written to an
        audit log.
      </p>

      <h2>Cookies</h2>
      <p>
        We use one session cookie to keep you signed in, and one to remember your language and
        theme choice. We do not use advertising trackers on this site.
      </p>
    </div>
  </div>
</section>
